<Base title="Troubleshooting" description='What to do when Sudo Play says "Sudo Play stopped in the background." or "Something went wrong. Please try again." on every button, and where the logs are.'>
  <h1>Troubleshooting</h1>
  <p class="lead">What to do when Sudo Play does not work as expected.</p>

  <h2>Every button in the window shows an error</h2>
  <p>Sudo Play runs a small PHP process in the background. Every button in the window goes through it. Sometimes something else stops that process, such as another app or macOS.</p>
  <p>Since 1.0.3, Sudo Play starts the process again on its own, after about a second. If the restart does not work, the app opens again by itself.</p>
  <p>If the process stops 3 times in 5 minutes, Sudo Play stops trying. The window then shows "Sudo Play stopped in the background. Press ⌘Q and open it again."</p>

  <h3>On 1.0.2 or earlier</h3>
  <p>Sudo Play does not start the process again. Nothing in the window works:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Play, Next, Surprise me and the genre and mood chips show "Something went wrong. Please try again."</li>
    <li>Settings shows "Could not open the settings. Please try again."</li>
    <li>Add a playlist shows "Could not open the browser."</li>
    <li>Quit shows "Could not quit. Please try again."</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The daily reminder still arrives, because it does not use this process. To get the automatic restart, <a href="/install/">install the current release</a>.</p>

  <h3>What to do</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Click the Sudo Play icon in the menu bar to open the window, then press <kbd>⌘</kbd> <kbd>Q</kbd>. You can also right-click the icon and choose <strong>Quit Sudo Play</strong>.</li>
    <li>Open Sudo Play again from Applications.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Nothing is lost. Your settings stay, and today's pick is the same. Next starts again from today's pick.</p>
  <p>If neither way works, open Terminal and run:</p>
  <pre><code>killall "Sudo Play"</code></pre>
  <p>Then open Sudo Play again.</p>

  <h2>Where the logs are</h2>
  <p>Sudo Play writes its log files in:</p>
  <pre><code>~/Library/Application Support/sudo-play/storage/logs/</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li><code>laravel-YYYY-MM-DD.log</code> has the app's warnings and errors. There is one file per day.</li>
    <li><code>electron.log</code> is new in 1.0.3. It comes from the part of the app that runs the window, and records when the background process stopped and started again. At about 1 MB, it becomes <code>electron.old.log</code>. Together, the two files stay at about 2 MB.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>On 1.0.2 or earlier, the problem above writes nothing to the log. So the log may be empty even when every button fails.</p>
</Base>
